    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d370">

                <pb facs="0371" n="347" sameAs="frus:frus1864p4/pg347"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Haldeman.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 39.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1864-03-31"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 31, 1864</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi>Your despatch No. 44, of the 8th instant,
                    has been received, and your graphic account of the late popular tumult in
                    Stockholm, occasioned by the stand taken by Count Manderstrom on the question of
                    the war now raging in Denmark, has been read with much interest.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jacob S. Haldeman</hi>, Esq., &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c</hi>., &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.,
                            &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.<hi rendition="#italic">,
                            Stockholm.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
